Dual V1/V2 entrypoint and package.json ./server export for opencode-background-agents.

Upstream dist/index.js exports default function BackgroundAgentsPlugin (V1),
which OpenCode V2 rejects:
  Plugin must export a default definition with an id and an effect or setup function.
Additionally, package.json defines an "exports" map with only ".", causing
OpenCode 2.3.0 Host.resolve() to resolve via package exports and bypass the
root server.js shim unless "./server" is also exported and "./dist/index.js"
provides the dual V1/V2 default object.

The V2 `setup(ctx)` below ports the V1 hook map onto the V2 hook API:
  tool                                    -> ctx.tool.transform()
  experimental.chat.system.transform      -> ctx.session.hook("context")
  experimental.session.compacting         -> ctx.session.hook("compaction")
  event                                   -> ctx.event.subscribe()

